===Etymology 1===
From {{inh-lite|zh|sit-pro|*lwi(j)||[[flow]]; [[stream]]|sort=水00}} ({{zh-ref|Benedict, 1974}}; {{zh-ref|Coblin, 1986}}; {{zh-ref|Handel, 1998}}; {{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}; STEDT). Cognate with {{cog-lite|lus|lui||stream; [[brook]]; [[river]]}}, {{cog-lite|ctd|||tr=luːi³|stream; river}}, {{cog-lite|kac|lawi||to flow (as [[water]])}}.

{{cog-lite|och|-}} {{och-l|水|tr=lhuiʔ}}, as reconstructed by Schuessler, is {{cog-lite|sit}} root's endoactive derivation with suffix ''*-ʔ'', meaning "that which is flowing"; its voiceless initial suggests the presence of a nominalizing prefix ''*k-'' or ''*s-''. Another derivative from the {{cog-lite|sit}} root is possibly {{och-l|泫|tr=winʔ|gloss=to flow}} (minimally reconstructed).

Compare also areal etymon {{cog-lite|mkh-pro|sc=Latinx|*lujʔ ~ luuj() ~ luəj() ~ ləəj()||to [[wade]]; to [[swim]]}}.

Alternatively, {{zh-ref|Gong (1995)}} reconstructs {{cog-lite|och|-}} ''*hljədx'' and compares it to {{cog-lite|bo|sc=Tibt|ཆུ||tr=chu|water}}, which STEDT derives from {{cog-lite|sit-pro|*tsju||water; [[liquid]]; [[bodily fluid]]}}. {{zh-ref|Baxter and Sagart (2014)}}, employing evidence from {{w|Proto-Min}}, reconstructs {{cog-lite|och|-}} ''*s.turʔ'' and compares it to {{cog-lite|sit-pro|*twəj||to flow; to [[suppurate]]}}, which is likely related to {{m-lite|sit-pro|*m-t(w)əj-n ~ m-ti-s||water; fluid; to [[soak]]; to be wet}} (STEDT). Like {{zh-ref|Gong (1995)}}, {{zh-ref|Sagart (2017)}} compares it to {{cog-lite|bo|sc=Tibt|ཆུ|tr=chu}}, but he also compares it to {{cog-lite|brx|sc=Deva|दै|tr=dwi}}, {{cog-lite|lus|tui}}, {{cog-lite|kar-pro|sc=Latinx|*thejᴬ}}, all of which STEDT derives from {{cog-lite|sit-pro|*m-t(w)əj-n ~ m-ti-s}}. Handel deems derivations from {{cog-lite|sit-pro|*tsju}} or {{m-lite|sit-pro|*m-t(w)əj-n ~ m-ti-s}} unlikely because of phonological issues (STEDT).

