===Etymology 1===
<div style="float:right;">
{{wp|lang=ja}}
{{wp|Water}}
</div>
{{ja-kanjitab|みず|yomi=k}}

{{IPAfont|⟨mi<sub>1</sub>du⟩}} → *{{IPAchar-lite|/mʲidu/}} → {{IPAchar-lite|/mid͡zu/}} → {{IPAchar-lite|/mizu/}}

From {{inh-lite|ja|ojp|-|sort=みず}}, from {{inh-lite|ja|jpx-pro|sc=Latinx|*mentu|sort=みず}}. Cognate with {{cog-lite|jpx-ryu-pro|sc=Latinx|*medu}}.

Possibly cognate with {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|瑞||tr=mizu|[[freshness]], [[youth]]}}.

Possible cognate with {{cog-lite|tuw-pro|sc=Latinx|*mū}}, {{cog-lite|juc|木克|tr=mu-ke|ts=muke}}, {{cog-lite|mnc|sc=mnc-Mong|ᠮᡠᡴᡝ|tr=muke}}, {{cog-lite|zkg|sc=Hani|買||tr=*me|river; water}}, {{cog-lite|mn|sc=Cyrl|мөрөн||tr=mörön|river}}, {{cog-lite|ko|sc=Kore|물||tr=mul|water}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|みず|acc=0|acc_ref=DJR}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|みず|hhira=みづ}}

# [[water]] {{gloss-lite|sometimes [[cold]] and/or [[fresh]]}}
#: {{syn-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|ウオーター|tr=uōtā|ウォーター|tr2=wōtā|がっこ|tr3=gakko|q3=Tsugaru}}
#: {{ant-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|湯|tr1=yu|pos1=specifically meaning "hot water"}}
# [[drinking water]]
#: {{syn-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|飲水|tr=insui, nomimizu|飲用水|tr2=in'yōsui|飲料水|tr3=inryōsui}}
# a [[fluid]], [[liquid]]
#: {{syn-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|液体|tr=ekitai}}
# a [[flood]]
#: {{syn-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|大水|tr=ōmizu|洪水|tr2=kōzui|出水|tr3=shussui}}
# {{lb|ja|sumo|sort=みす}} {{short for|ja|水入り|tr=mizuiri|dot=:|sort=みず}} [[halt]]ing
# {{lb|ja|sumo|sort=みす}} {{short for|ja|力水|tr=chikara mizu|dot=:}} water [[offer]]ed to [[sumo]] [[wrestler]]s before a [[bout]]

====Usage notes====
Note that, while ''mizu'' is the most general Japanese term for “{{m-lite|en|water}}”, it does refer specifically to “{{m-lite|en|[[water]] that is not [[hot]]|[[water]] that is not [[hot]]}}”.  Meanwhile, the word {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|湯|tr=yu}} refers specifically to “{{m-lite|en|hot water}}”.  Consider {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|水風呂||tr=mizu-buro|[[cold]]-[[water]] [[bath]]}}, contrasting with {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|風呂||tr=furo|pos=implying hot water|[[bath]]}}.

